Third-party content in web/test/fixtures/
=========================================

These .html files are unmodified captures of Telegram's own public preview pages
(https://t.me/s/<channel>), saved so that a change in Telegram's markup fails a
test instead of a live page (PUBLIC.md §3).

They contain content owned by Telegram and by the channel authors — page markup,
inlined CSS, post text and CDN media URLs. That content is NOT Lucian Labs' to
license, and it is excluded from the MIT grant in the LICENSE file at the root of
this repository. It is included here for interoperability testing only.

  telegram.html, telegram.before-435.html   t.me/s/telegram — Telegram's own
                                            announcement channel, © Telegram
  tastycrow.html, tgs_dankcoin.html         channels belonging to this project's
                                            author, captured with consent

If you fork this repository and do not need the parser tests, delete this
directory. If you need fixtures of your own, capture them from channels you
control rather than redistributing someone else's.
